# Jira Boards: the active sprint as a kanban — the board and sprint
# chips, the avatar cluster seeded to me, the four columns with their
# counts, the cursor's card, > expanding a card, the detail modal, the
# team picker, and the Backlog tab.
# The pane's token bucket, private to this file. Without it the
# bucket may resolve to a machine-wide shared file
# ($MNML_SHARED_STATE_DIR/jira-ratelimit.json), where anything
# else on the machine can drain it and leave the pane on
# `loading…` for a minute — a flake with no cause on screen.
# env: JIRA_RATELIMIT_STATE=${MNML_E2E_WORKSPACE}/jira-bucket.json
# env: JIRA_API_TOKEN=fake-token
# env: JIRA_BASE_URL=@${MNML_E2E_WORKSPACE}/jira.url
# The fake takes port 0 and writes the URL it landed on to `jira.url`;
# `JIRA_BASE_URL=@<file>` is how the pane reads it, so nothing here ever
# picks a port and two runs of the corpus never collide. The config's
# `.jira_url` is the placeholder that override replaces.
shell "$MNML_FAKE_JIRA" --port 0 --url-file jira.url --life-secs 180 --quiet --pid-file fake-jira.pid >/dev/null 2>&1 &
wait 500
write sdk/mnml-sdk/build.zig ""
write integrations/jira/build.zig ""
write integrations/jira/manifest.zon ".{ .id = \"jira_boards\", .label = \"Jira Boards\", .version = \"0.2.0\", .binary = \"$MNML_JIRA\", .category = \"tracker\", .commands = .{ .{ .id = \"jira_boards.open\", .title = \"Jira Boards\", .args = .{ \"--only\", \"boards\" } } } }"
write .mnml/integrations/jira/config.zon ".{ .jira_url = \"https://jira.invalid\", .email = \"fake@acme.com\", .refresh_interval_secs = 0, .rate = .{ .per_sec = 1000, .burst = 1000 }, .team_field_id = \"customfield_10056\", .tabs = .{ .{ .name = \"Sprint\", .kind = .board_active_sprint, .project = \"ENG\", .board_id = 7 }, .{ .name = \"Backlog\", .kind = .board_backlog, .project = \"ENG\" } } }"
command integrations.show_in_dev
expect screen contains "INTEGRATIONS"
drag 30 5 60 5
expect screen contains "[dev] Jira Boards  0.2.0  not installed"
key i
expect screen contains "installed jira_boards from"
wait 4000
# The corpus lays its screens out at full width: the pane opens as a tab,
# not beside whatever the install left active (`integrations.open_as`).
command integrations.open_as_tab
command jira_boards.open
command view.toggle_tree
command view.focus_pane
# The sprint from the board; the assignee filter seeded to me shows 3 of 9.
expect screen contains "JIRA BOARDS (3 of 9)"
expect screen contains "1 Sprint"
expect screen contains "2 Backlog"
expect screen contains " board: Checkout board "
expect screen contains " sprint: Sprint 4 "
expect screen contains " SB "
expect screen contains " [?] "
expect screen contains " quick filters "
expect screen contains " settings "
expect screen contains " To Do ("
expect screen contains " In Progress ("
expect screen contains " Testing ("
expect screen contains " Done ("
expect screen contains "ENG-1"
expect screen contains "Checkout rewrite"
expect screen contains "· Ada Lovelace"
expect screen lacks "ENG-6"
# > expands the cursor's card: label chips and the hint line.
key shift+.
expect screen contains "#checkout"
expect screen contains "(click card for full"
key shift+.
expect screen lacks "(click card for full"
# D: the detail modal with the field table and the description.
key shift+d
expect screen contains "ENG-1 · Checkout rewrite  [In Progress]"
expect screen contains "Assignee    : Ada Lovelace"
expect screen contains "The umbrella for the checkout work."
key esc
expect screen lacks "Assignee    : Ada Lovelace"
# T: the team picker over the components, labels and team values seen.
key shift+t
expect screen contains "filter kanban by team"
expect screen contains "— Clear team —"
expect screen contains "Apollo"
key esc
# The Backlog tab: the tickets in no sprint — two, neither mine, so the
# seeded assignee filter shows none of them until it is cleared.
key 2
expect screen contains "JIRA BOARDS (0 of 2)"
expect screen contains " To Do (0)"
expect screen lacks "ENG-1 "
key q
wait 500
key x
expect screen lacks "1 Sprint"
# Uninstall before leaving: `--install` wrote the three manifests into
# the corpus's one shared data root, and x removes one row at a time —
# the first manifest row each time, alphabetically.
command integrations.show_installed
expect screen contains "Installed (7)"
# The three manifests sort last: End reaches each in turn.
key end
key x
expect screen contains "Remove Jira Work?"
key r
expect screen contains "removed jira_work"
command integrations.show_installed
key end
key x
expect screen contains "Remove Jira Fix Versions?"
key r
expect screen contains "removed jira_fix_versions"
command integrations.show_installed
key end
key x
expect screen contains "Remove Jira Boards?"
key r
expect screen contains "removed jira_boards"
expect screen contains "Installed (4)"
shell kill "$(cat fake-jira.pid)" 2>/dev/null || true
